# Diagnostic renders. ANCHORED to the repository root with a leading slash, because the
# debug tools write them here and nowhere else. Unanchored, these match at any depth: the
# unanchored `land-*.png` silently swallowed a vendored Cesium asset
# (viewer/public/vendor/cesium/Assets/Textures/maki/land-use.png), and a 394-of-395 vendor
# would have committed clean and passed unnoticed. Keep the slashes.
/*.ppm
/plates.png
/margins.png
/motion.png
/land-*.png
/base.png
/tectonic.png
/macro.png
/harbour-*.png
/bottom*.png
/grid-*.png
/grid-*.ppm
/fine-*.png
/fine-*.ppm
/look-*.png
/look-*.ppm
/patch.*
/chartlook.*
/chart-*.png
/relief.png
/safety*.png

/target/
crates/*/target/

# A real Evennia game database, copied here for slice 2a's integration proof. NEVER COMMITTED.
#
# This is a live game's data -- accounts, characters, everything they have written. It is here
# because slice 2a's claim is that a real, messy, long-lived game gains a planet without losing
# anything, and that claim cannot be tested against a fixture built for it. It is a COPY of a
# backup; the original is never opened.
#
# The repository's commits feed a public channel, so an accidental `git add -A` would publish
# somebody's game. Anchored, and the directory is ignored whole rather than by extension, so a
# journal, a WAL file or an extracted table is covered too.
/fixtures/dragonsire/
routes/
